---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/08-04/', manual='https://mpt.eecs.yorku.ca/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/Operators-Manual.pdf', sheet='https://www.epfl.ch/research/facilities/cmi/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/FINEPLACER_lambda_specifications_en.pdf';
---
<Layout pageTitle="FINEPLACER lambda · geometric flip-chip alignment" description="Use virtual optical fiducials and a manual flip arm to verify the geometric overlap of an inert die and carrier." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment fp">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/08-04/">← Equipment 08-04</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#fp-reference">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">08-04 · OPTICAL DIE REGISTRATION / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Finetech FINEPLACER lambda A7</h2><p>Register an inert face-down die against an asymmetric carrier. The default fiducials can correct the global offset and rotation, but one bump is misplaced on purpose.</p></header>
<div class="fp-grid"><section><h3>Manual A7 fixture</h3><div id="fp-view" aria-label="Orbitable model of the original FINEPLACER lambda A7 with optical head, swing arm, air-bearing table, and separate controller"></div><div class="bar"><button data-fp-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-fp-view="stage">Stage close-up</button><button data-fp-view="rear">Controller rear</button></div><p id="fp-ready" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The turquoise optics control and amber arm control invoke the same actions as the buttons.</p></section>
<section><h3>Registration exercise</h3><div class="fields"><label>Initial die X (µm)<input id="fp-x" type="number" min="-250" max="250" step="any" value="120"/></label><label>Initial die Y (µm)<input id="fp-y" type="number" min="-250" max="250" step="any" value="-55"/></label><label>Initial rotation (° CCW)<input id="fp-theta" type="number" min="-5" max="5" step="any" value="2"/></label><label class="check"><input id="fp-defect" type="checkbox" checked/> Shift bump E by 120 µm</label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="fp-align" class="primary">Align fiducials</button><button id="fp-optics">Park optics</button><button id="fp-arm">Lower arm (dry)</button><button id="fp-record">Record placement</button><button id="fp-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="fp-status" aria-live="polite">Inert die and carrier loaded. Align fiducials, park optics, lower the arm, then record the dry placement check.</p><output id="fp-correction"></output><canvas id="fp-overlay" width="720" height="500" aria-label="Amber carrier fiducials and pads overlaid with green measured die features"></canvas></section></div>
<section><h3>Geometric connection map</h3><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Bump → pad</th><th>Center offset (µm)</th><th>Bump area on intended pad</th><th>Geometric status</th></tr></thead><tbody id="fp-pairs"></tbody></table></div><div class="bar"><button id="fp-json" disabled>Export placement JSON</button><button id="fp-csv" disabled>Export pair CSV</button></div><p>A geometric pass requires at least 50% bump-area overlap and no overlap with another pad. This threshold is a teaching choice, not a prediction of a bond or continuity, and recording does not alter the specimen.</p></section>
<section id="fp-reference"><h3>References and evidence</h3>
<figure><img width="850" height="270" src={base+'reference.svg'} loading="lazy" alt="Original side schematic showing the A7 die held on the pivot arm, dual-view prism and carrier stage"/><figcaption>Original simulator diagram, not a photograph or traced engineering drawing. The <a href={manual+'#page=6'}>Finetech Rev. 1.1 lateral diagram, p. 6</a> identifies the camera, stationary beam splitter, 90° pivot path and working level. The <a href={manual+'#page=17'}>p. 17 photos</a> establish the side-shifting optics and arm interlock.</figcaption></figure>
<p><a href={sheet+'#page=1'}>Manufacturer overall front photograph (May 2012 lambda datasheet)</a> · <a href={manual+'#page=15'}>Rev. 1.1 table/micrometer close-up</a> · <a href={manual+'#page=44'}>Rev. 1.1 technical dimensions and rear connector inventory</a>. The separate controller’s rear connector locations and undocumented parts are inferred, not measured. No production hardware photograph is embedded.</p>
<div class="fp-grid"><figure><img width="600" height="400" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original front reconstruction of optical tower, working table and controller"/><figcaption>Original front render. Compared with the manufacturer’s front photo for the upright camera, black support, bronze table and side illumination. The controller is separate.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="600" height="400" src={base+'side.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original side close-up of the positioning table and optical assembly"/><figcaption>Original working-area render. Compared with the manual’s table photograph and side views for layout, not mechanical dimensions.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Documented or reference value</th><th>Actual / use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Configuration</td><td>Legacy A7 manual, standard VAS and sliding clearance; not lambda 2</td><td>Geometry only; optional heat, process gas, force and dispense systems omitted.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Base and standard camera height</td><td>620 × 420 mm base, 700 mm bench-to-top; separate controller 290 × 310 × 143 mm</td><td>Metric GLB anchors, manual p. 44. Camera-module height may vary.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Working area; fine theta travel</td><td>190 × 52 mm (manual p. 44); ±5° (datasheet p. 2)</td><td>Exercise limits ±250 µm translation and ±5°; no instrumentation accuracy claim. A7 is rated &lt;1 µm in the manual, distinct from numerical tolerance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent registration</td><td>True +120/−55 µm, +2°</td><td>Fit recovers the injected transform within 10⁻⁹; inverse θ −2° and <a href={base+'verification.json'}>unrounded XY verified</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Known good and bad pairs</td><td>4 full overlaps; E has 0% at 120 µm residual</td><td>4/5 pass, E open geometrically; disabling the defect gives 5/5. All tolerances are computational, not hardware calibration.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Inputs are three labeled fiducial pairs, five circular bumps (35 µm radius), matching pads (55 µm), and a rigid shift and rotation. Coordinates are micrometers in the carrier plane, +X right and +Y away from the operator; the die is already presented face-down, so no second reflection is applied. The simulator centers the observed and target points, finds the least-squares rotation by <code>atan2(Σ cross, Σ dot)</code>, restores translation from the centroids, and computes circle-lens area divided by bump area. Coincident fiducials, invalid ranges and lowering the arm over the optics are rejected.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={base+'fineplacer-lambda.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Locked reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-placement.json'}>Output schema/example</a>. No physical headset, actual bonding, or downstream reader is claimed.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/08-04/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.fp{max-width:76rem}.fp .fp-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.fp section{min-width:0;margin:.8rem 0;padding:.8rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.fp .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.fp .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem}.fp label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.fp label.check{display:flex;flex-direction:row;align-items:center}.fp input,.fp button{font:inherit;min-width:0;max-width:100%;min-height:2.4em;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.15rem;padding:.32em .54em;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel)}.fp input[type=checkbox]{min-height:1em}.fp button{cursor:pointer}.fp button:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}.fp .primary{background:#245350;color:white}.fp #fp-status.error{color:#a54a34}.fp #fp-view{height:clamp(265px,31vw,410px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.fp #fp-view :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%}.fp #fp-overlay,.fp figure img{width:100%;height:auto}.fp #fp-correction{display:block;min-height:2.3rem;font-family:monospace}.fp .scroll{overflow:auto}.fp table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.9rem}.fp th,.fp td{padding:.45rem;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.fp figure{margin:1rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.fp .fp-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
